export anchor HumanistStyle:
    number: 208
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Humanist
    idea: A warm, serious workspace set in a humanist sans, with soft ivory surfaces, clay accents, rounded but restrained shapes and plain friendly words.
    base: light
    palette:
        ivory: #fbf8f4, the page, resting fields and fact tiles
        white: #ffffff, cards, the top bar and the style sheet
        oat: #f3ece4, the navigation band
        cocoa: #2a2522, text
        stone: #625a55, secondary text, dates and chart axis
        sand: #e9dfd5, borders and dividers, never text
        clay: #a8441f, the primary button, links, progress rings, the chart line and focus
        blush: #f8e9e1, the focus halo and the logo disc
        peach: #f1d9cc, the chart area fill, never text
        sage: #3d6b55, KPI icons on #e7f0ea
        green: #2f6a4b, On track on #e7f0ea with a circle and check
        amber: #8a5000, At risk on #fbefd9 with a rounded triangle
        roseRed: #a92f3a, Behind and the overdue note on #fbe9ea with a rounded square and back chevron
    type:
        One humanist stack, Segoe UI, Optima, Candara, Gill Sans, Noto Sans,
        Trebuchet MS, sans-serif. Body is 15px at 1.6. The greeting is 30px
        at 600, week totals 28px, KPI values 24px, section titles 17px at
        600, project names 16px at 600 and meta lines 13px in stone. No
        capitals styling anywhere.
    layout:
        A white top bar holds the brand with a clay sun on a blush disc, a
        wide round search field in the middle, the clay New project
        button, a rounded bell and the user with a lilac initials disc.
        Under it an oat band holds the six nav links as a segmented
        control, a pale rounded tray with Home as a raised white tab. The
        date and greeting sit above three columns, 260px, flexible and
        300px. The left column stacks a rose tinted note saying 4 tasks
        are overdue with a short friendly line, then a Your week card
        listing the four KPIs with a sage icon tile, label and value per
        line, split by dashed rules. The middle card lists the projects,
        each row with a clay progress ring holding the percent, the name
        with team and task count, and on the right the status chip over
        the due date with days to go. The right card, What the team did,
        lists activity with pastel initials discs. A full width chart
        card follows with title and the two week totals on the left and a
        smooth clay line over a peach area on the right, the second week
        softly shaded. Below 1150px the activity card drops under the
        projects. On phones everything is one column, KPIs two by two and
        chips move under each project name.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 16 to 24px gaps, 20px card padding and 32px above the content.
    density: Comfortable. 76px project rows with rings, easy to scan.
    corners: 16px cards, 12px buttons, fields and rows, 10px tabs, a fully round search field.
    borders: 1px warm sand on cards, with dashed dividers inside the KPI list.
    shadows: A faint two layer shadow, 0 2px 8px at 5 percent cocoa.
    icons:
        Rounded 1.8px outline icons at 20px. Status uses an outlined circle
        with a check for On track, a rounded outlined triangle with a bang
        for At risk and a rounded outlined square with a back chevron for
        Behind, always with the word in a tinted chip.
    focus: A 2px clay outline offset 2px plus a 5px blush halo. Fields show the clay border and halo only.
    tone: Warm and plain, such as Your week, What the team did and Worth a look before anything else today.
